33. Find First Non-Null Value

PySpark:

from pyspark.sql.functions import first

df.groupBy("customer_id") \
  .agg(
      first(
      "email",
      ignorenulls=True
      )
  )

SQL:

SELECT customer_id,
FIRST_VALUE(email)
IGNORE NULLS
OVER(
PARTITION BY customer_id
ORDER BY update_date
)
FROM customer;
